\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{The continuum commutator}
\date{2026-11-13}

\p{The continuum commutator in \ref{fdip-00AP} is
#{\bigl[\tfrac{d}{dx},x\bigr]=1}.
Physics writes the same relation as #{[p,x]=-\ui\hbar} with
#{p=-\ui\hbar\,d/dx}. That factor makes the derivative Hermitian.
Multiplication by a root-of-unity character, the cyclic shift and
the powers of that root generate the algebra. No unit bivector of
a plane, and no central pseudoscalar of square #{-1}, replaces
that factor.}
